  "id": "COMPOUND:30325 - PROTEIN:4953",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 8-O-(3-Hydroxy-3-Methylbutyryl)Desacylcynaropicrin may interact with HEp-2 cells. This compound targets a splicing factor, proline- and glutamine-rich, which is a key component in the splicing of pre-mRNA. This splicing factor is also a target of oxybenzone, a well-documented compound that has been shown to influence cellular processes, including gene expression. The interaction between 8-O-(3-Hydroxy-3-Methylbutyryl)Desacylcynaropicrin and HEp-2 is thus mediated through a chain of targets that ultimately affects splicing and potentially cellular function in the HEp-2 cell line. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and HEp-2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
